From: Paweł Phan <szop.hektar_1w@icloud.com>
Subject: [PATCH] package/busybox: take fixes of ash, awk, tar and udhcpc

SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only
SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2026 Paweł Phan <szop.hektar_1w@icloud.com>

BusyBox's fixes of 2026 for applets the image holds, which no release
carries yet (1.38.0 predates them), as patches 0021 to 0025 after the
release's own:

- ash: an out-of-bounds read in ifsbreakup() after an expansion that
  failed (CVE-2026-38754), backported to 1.37.0;
- awk: a one-byte heap overflow in next_token() when a string ends the
  program;
- tar: file names in the verbose listing printed with their control
  characters;
- udhcpc: the magic cookie read before the packet is known to hold it, and
  the minimum size checked before the length is cut to the IP header's.

The two of udhcpc concern what a DHCP server of the network sends. Applets
the image leaves out are not patched (ssl_server, httpd, dpkg, the
volume_id probers, libpwdgrp, here strings of 1.38). The release's ash and
awk tests give the same results with and without them.

Signed-off-by: Paweł Phan <szop.hektar_1w@icloud.com>
